{"title":"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Exactly three of the interior angles of a convex polygon are obtuse. What is the maximum number of sides of such a polygon?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbc3d1399a390317b8d5b98faace5f2d4d8bf10.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)\\ } 4 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ }5 \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\  } 6 \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\  } 7 \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\  }8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"342\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that such a polygon has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> sides. Let the three obtuse angle measures, in degrees, be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/c/42c9c0367f6081c0050147aa1bd5fd7178fff1e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$o_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/d/38de031b7771b317f699e994d332a4dde80f8ce2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$o_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/a/1eac894b3f2f9102a6e17c78ecfbc2b12c7a3ef2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$o_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/5/7b5e338b812a971809090f313a91304847c2f588.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n-3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> acute angle measures, again in degrees, be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/813f9bd7602b60281c8d3311edf1bee5ee7a5bfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2,a_3, \\dotsc a_{n-3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"137\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/0/d700abf4d57e5945e5033cee7de8d77e8b84c7a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90 &lt; o_i &lt; 180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"17\" /> for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/4/9043a982b771715f9a5a66da32d24d46af504641.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3(90) = 270 &lt; o_1+o_2+o_3 &lt; 3(180) = 540,\\]\" width=\"340\" height=\"18\" /> and similarly, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/e/c4e0249211a9fdc4e7ccdb832911f81f98cab32c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0 &lt; a_i &lt; 90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"93\" height=\"17\" /> for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/7/d378272ceb73f5bd3e60f81feeba16510407dd73.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[0 &lt; a_1+a_2+a_3+\\dotsb+a_{n-3} &lt; 90(n-3) = 90n-270.\\]\" width=\"434\" height=\"18\" />\nIt follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7c22edaf832406f2f77a8cb6ddc28b17b2d10b2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[270+0 &lt; o_1+o_2+o_3+a_1+a_2+a_3+\\dotsb+a_{n-3} &lt; 540+90n-270,\\]\" width=\"538\" height=\"16\" /> and recalling that the sum of the interior angle measures of an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />-gon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/0/af0accb0cadb6f02bcc82dd1801842cd3bda9ae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180(n-2) = 180n-360$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"197\" height=\"20\" />, this reduces to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56ce822b1e7e5156f6c0534533b6846c117299f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$270 &lt; 180n-360 &lt; 90n+270$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"244\" height=\"15\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb09453cc7254b71956cecaf046b86e85797179.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{540}{180} &lt; n &lt; \\frac{270+360}{90} \\iff 3 &lt; n &lt; 7,\\]\" width=\"304\" height=\"38\" /> so an upper bound is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/2/99299c9615dbad662d0ec562fccc41c61b4a9914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\leq 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"46\" height=\"16\" />, and it is easy to check that this bound can be attained by e.g. a convex hexagon with a right angle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> acute angles, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> obtuse angles, as shown below:\n</p><p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:HrKCfF2ETNSQSy3uGlkg_hexagonsurvey1.gif\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/3/37/HrKCfF2ETNSQSy3uGlkg_hexagonsurvey1.gif/100px-HrKCfF2ETNSQSy3uGlkg_hexagonsurvey1.gif\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"100\" height=\"91\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/3/37/HrKCfF2ETNSQSy3uGlkg_hexagonsurvey1.gif/150px-HrKCfF2ETNSQSy3uGlkg_hexagonsurvey1.gif 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/3/37/HrKCfF2ETNSQSy3uGlkg_hexagonsurvey1.gif 2x\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>Accordingly, the maximum possible number of sides of such a polygon is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/1/5a14557e0aab30919b3d48a2cb85ae930396a713.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\text{(C)} \\ 6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"53\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME\" title=\"1985 AHSME\">1985 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1985 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1985\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1985 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1985_AHSME_Pro